messages:
elaine: Quick heads-up — I'm opening a small batch of docs PRs to tidy up function-calling + structured-output examples. Goal: clearer JSON Schema examples, explicit guardrails, and paired SDK snippets (py/js). Will try to merge by EOD Thu; need reviewers and a couple quick edits. PRs: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/412 (examples) and /413 (snippets). Copy of suggested schema below. Can @sam and @jordan take a look?

doc-bot: link-checker: PR 412: link-check passed :white_check_mark:

sam: thanks — will review tonight. quick note: our style guide prefers explicit `additionalProperties: false` on response schemas. also we should add a tiny comment about fallback parsing for partial outputs. :eyes:

jordan: +1. also prefer example that shows both `envelope` and `compact` response shapes, with a small parser snippet that tries envelope first then falls back. users keep getting confused about optional fields.

elaine: agreed. here's the schema I drafted for the example (embed into docs/guides/function-calling.md):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "action": { "type": "string", "description": "the action to run" },
    "args": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "user_id": { "type": "string" },
        "items": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }
      },
      "required": ["user_id"],
      "additionalProperties": false
    }
  },
  "required": ["action"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

elaine: and the tiny parse-fallback example I want to add to the SDK snippet section (docs/snippets/sdk/python_function_call.md):

```py
# try envelope -> compact -> basic json
try:
    out = parse_envelope(response)
except ParseError:
    try:
        out = parse_compact(response)
    except ParseError:
        out = heuristics_fallback(response)
```

kevin: quick product note — make sure the examples show a clear reason to pick envelope vs compact (latency vs simplicity). maybe a one-line callout.

sam: will add `additionalProperties` mention and a short paragraph about guardrails (limit free-form fields, prefer enumerated enums where possible). also will update the JS SDK snippet to match the py fallback example.

jordan: small nit: in the examples we use `structuredOutput: true` elsewhere — can we be consistent? either mention both or normalize to `structured_output` in docs.

elaine: good catch. let's normalize to `structured_output` (snake_case) across the examples. I'll update PR 412 before merging.

doc-bot: deploy-preview: docs site build succeeded for PR 412 (preview available at https://deploy-preview-412--docs.redwood.ai).

sam: awesome — will push review comments on 412 and open a small follow-up for the JS snippet if I need help.

elaine: thanks all! Action items: sam -> add guardrail paragraph + JS fallback snippet; jordan -> sanity-check envelope/compact wording; kevin -> add single product callout; I'll update the schema and rename flag to `structured_output`. Target merge: Thu EOD. :rocket:
